    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (71.95) and **Jackson Merrill** (67.27), our two most potent plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Gausman; despite the tough SP_xERA, his position in the two-hole and an extreme propensity for stolen bases against a slower delivery profile makes him a must-start. **Jackson Merrill** remains a top-tier asset, as the combination of an favorable wind blowing out and his advantageous spot in the lineup elevates his output against Brazob\u00e1n. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.47) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.74) round out our core; while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a slightly more challenging arm in Baz, his pedigree and order placement keep his floor exceptionally high.\n\nWe are hunting upside in the middle-infield and outfield, specifically leaning on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.40) and **Josh Jung** (60.61). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sees a significant boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Soroka, while **Josh Jung** provides consistent value by maintaining neutral platoon stability against Cantillo. The toughest roster decision today was excluding **Nolan Schanuel** (44.18) from the utility spot. While his base projection was solid, he was ultimately benched because the SP_xERA for Sheehan (3.31) created a difficult hurdle for a high-AVG profile like his, pushing him just below the efficiency threshold of our high-upside starters like **Miguel Vargas** (48.25) and **Miguel Andujar** (45.26). \n\nRisk mitigation remains a priority as we manage our game caps. **Liam Hicks** (46.39) is on the active roster but requires careful monitoring; his score is propped up by his leadoff status, yet he faces a decent arm in Jax. We are also wary of the conditions surrounding **Miguel Andujar**, whose score is highly sensitive to the wind; any shift in the breeze could render his start marginal. All other bench assets, including **Brayan Rocchio** and **Dominic Smith**, fell below our 40.0 floor due to unfavorable SP skill levels, signaling a disciplined approach to preserving our limited innings for high-probability days.",
